Program 1: Employee Salary Classification

Aim
To write a Python program to calculate employee net salary and classify the job role based on salary.

Algorithm
Start the program.
Define a function empcalc().
Input employee name.
Input employee age.
Input employee salary.
Calculate HRA = 35% of salary.
Calculate PF = 25% of salary.
Calculate net salary = salary + HRA + PF.
If net salary ≥ 30000 and ≤ 100000 → print "senior manager".
Else if net salary ≥ 20000 and ≤ 29000 → print "manager".
Else → print "front level job".
Return name, age, and net salary.
Call the function and store returned values.
Display employee name, age, and salary.
Stop the program.

code
def empcalc():
    name = input("enter name: ")
    age = int(input("enter age: "))
    sal = float(input("enter salary: "))

    hra = (35 * sal) / 100
    pf = (25 * sal) / 100
    netsal = sal + hra + pf

    if (netsal >= 30000) and (netsal <= 100000):
        print("senior manager")
    elif (netsal >= 20000) and (netsal <= 29000):
        print("manager")
    else:
        print("front level job")

    return name, age, netsal


name, age, netsal = empcalc()

print("employee name:", name)
print("employee age:", age)
print("employee salary:", netsal)

