Program 2: Tuple Operations

Aim
To write a Python program to perform various operations on a tuple.

Algorithm
Start the program.
Create a tuple t = (10, 20, 30, 40, 50).
Display the tuple.
Display first element.
Display last element.
Find and display length of tuple.
Count occurrences of an element.
Find index of an element.
Find maximum element.
Find minimum element.
Find sum of elements.
Check if an element is present.
Convert tuple to list.
Convert list back to tuple.
Stop the program.

code

t = (10, 20, 30, 40, 50)

print("tuple:", t)
print("first element:", t[0])
print("last element:", t[-1])
print("length:", len(t))
print("count of 20:", t.count(20))
print("index of 30:", t.index(30))
print("maximum:", max(t))
print("minimum:", min(t))
print("sum:", sum(t))
print("is 40 present?", 40 in t)

# conversion to list
l = list(t)
print("converted tuple to list:", l)

# convert list back to tuple
t2 = tuple(l)
print("list converted to tuple:", t2)

